---
import SectionHeading from "../shared/SectionHeading.astro";
---

<section class="border-t border-slate-100 bg-stone-50">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
    <SectionHeading
      eyebrow="Stage 7–8 · The Growth Loop"
      headline="This is where the process stops being a project and becomes a system."
      subhead="Performance feeds back into the plan — this is the same continuous-improvement cycle EverCompass runs on."
    />
    <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl space-y-5 text-lg text-slate-600">
      <p>
        <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-900"
          >Optimize — "Make it perform better."</strong
        > Once something is live, real performance data feeds back into the process.
        We look for bottlenecks, conversion friction, and testing opportunities —
        and act on what we find.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-900"
          >Grow — "Keep improving."</strong
        > Optimize is the work of a single cycle — testing and fixing what's in front
        of us right now. Grow is what happens over many cycles: your Growth System
        becomes an evolving system, not a one-time project, as EverJourneys keeps working
        through measure → learn → improve → repeat. This is the client-facing side
        of what EverCompass calls the Growth Loop — the same continuous cycle, seen
        from where you sit. Every stage of your process feeds the next one, so your
        system keeps compounding instead of resetting.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
